  "body": "Found while tracing #1224 (row 7, \"a setup whose own post does not serve its own machine - refused by name, nothing posted\").\n\n## What happens\n\n`mill_and_lathe()` in `crates/app/tests/setup_mounts_post.rs`: Setup1 on a bench mill (Face1), Setup2 on a bench lathe (`kind: lathe`, Facing2 - a turning Facing op with the TN-1600-0R8 insert). Give Setup2 its own post `Haas` (a milling dialect; `post_serves(\"Haas\", Kind::Lathe)` is false) and post one file per mount (`posting::post_mounts`). Nothing is refused. Setup2's file is:\n\n```\n%\n(Bench lathe)\nG21\n(SETUP: Setup2)\n(OPERATION: Facing2 - FACING - G54)\nG17 G90 G54 G40 G49 G80\n(T2 TN-1600-0R8 - TURNING INSERT D16)\nT2 M6\nG43 H2\nS3000 M3\nM8\nG0 X0 Y6.5 Z25\nG1 X0 Y6.5 Z16 F80\nG1 X0 Y6 Z16 F150\nG1 X0 Y-0.8 Z16 F150\n...\nM30\n```\n\nA milling program for a lathe: XY plane, a tool change with length offset, the TOOL spindle started at 3000 rpm, the facing pass written as Y moves at X0 (the meridian's radius on an axis a 2-axis lathe does not have), no G18, no diameter X, no G96/G50 or workholding ceiling. Posted silently - this is wrong output that passes.\n\n## Expected\n\nRefused by name before a line is written, as #1190 refuses the reverse (a milling op through a lathe post): a turning-family op (and anything else a lathe runs on the work spindle) may reach only a turning dialect. `post_serves` documents that a mismatched choice \"is not refused here ... the post refuses by name what it cannot express\" - the milling posts do not.\n\n## Scope\n\nReproduced with a setup's own post (#343/#388). The single-file post (`post_setup` -> `post_script_body`) runs the same pipeline with no such check, so a lathe document whose document post is a milling dialect is very likely the same (not run). Probably also any user `.cps` that is not a turning dialect (cf. #1199).\n\n## Pinning test\n\n`an_own_milling_post_on_a_lathe_setup_is_refused_by_name` in `crates/app/tests/setup_mounts_post.rs`, on branch `issue/1206-setup-machine-post-per-setup` (PR #1222), kept `#[ignore = \"#1232: ...\"]` until fixed.\n\nDone means: a turning op whose mount's post is not a turning dialect is refused by name (the op, the setup, the post) and nothing is written, in the per-mount and single-file posts; the pinning test runs un-ignored and green.\n\n",
